+// Report of one GDAKI window MR of a process under hold or in spare mode (a fail-fast process writes nothing, as hk):
+// strict = the ordering asked of gdakiRegMr, forced = the restore request makes it strict whatever the flags,
+// flag_strict = the window flags asked for strict, ro = IBV_ACCESS_RELAXED_ORDERING in the access flags gdakiRegMr actually
+// registered with (its own output, not a second evaluation). The pilot reads these lines (EXPERIMENT.md 3: every window MR
+// of a process that asks for the restore forced and ro=0; none forced with NCCL_GIN_RESTORE=0).
+static void gdakiRsWinReport(int rank, size_t size, bool flagStrict, bool strict, int access) {
